<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurūgo</span></b> , ĭnis,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>f</i> [aurum].
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The jaundice</i> (from its color),
					<i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 4, 8, 13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurugo, quam quidam regium, quidam arquatum
					morbum vocant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 110</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">127</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 85</span></i>; cf. Apul. Orth.
			§ 41; hence, <i>sickly look</i>, <i>paleness</i>, Vulg Jer. 30,
			6.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			plants, <i>mildew</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Par.
				6, 28</span></i>; ib. Amos, 4, 9.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
